('Rozbrat', NULL, 'art', 'Rozbrat is a long-running anarchist self-managed social centre in Jeżyce in Poznań, Poland.', NULL, '1h', '€', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Rozbrat_plakat_demo.jpg?width=1024', 52.4175454, 16.9183482, 'Kazimierza Pułaskiego 21a, 60-607, Poznan, Poland', 'https://www.rozbrat.org', 'way/244668647', 'en:Rozbrat', 'kolektyw Rozbrat · CC BY-SA 3.0 (via Wikimedia Commons)', 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Lake Malta', 'Jezioro Maltańskie', 'outdoor', 'Lake Malta, known also as the Maltański Reservoir, is an artificial lake in Poznań, Poland. It was formed in 1952 as a result of the damming of the Cybina River. It is about 2.2 km long, which makes the lake the biggest man-made lake of the city. The water is 3.1 m deep on average with a maximum about 5 m. There are a number of recreational attractions along the edge of the lake including:an artificial ski slope,
an artificial ice rink,
a zoological garden,
Kolejka Parkowa Maltanka - a narrow gauge railway,
the Mound of Freedom,
seasonal bikes rental - MaltaBike', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Malta_Trybuny_Pozna%C5%84_RB1.JPG?width=1024', 52.4038661, 16.9620283, 'Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'relation/7550595', 'en:Lake Malta', 'CC BY-SA 3.0 (via Wikimedia Commons)', 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Cytadela Park', 'Park Cytadela', 'outdoor', 'The Citadel Park in Poznań, Poland is a large park on the site of Fort Winiary, a 19th-century fortified area north of the city centre. It contains a military museum, military cemeteries, and the remains of some of the fortifications. It lies within the Stare Miasto district of the city, south of Winogrady.', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Cytadela_Pozna%C5%84_wej%C5%9Bcie_g%C5%82%C3%B3wne.jpg?width=1024', 52.4215502, 16.9345022, '61-663, Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'way/23003645', 'en:Citadel Park', 'Rzuwig · CC BY 3.0 (via Wikimedia Commons)', 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Wilson Park', 'Park Wilsona', 'outdoor', 'Elegant landscaped park surrounding the Palm House.', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', NULL, 52.398336, 16.9032723, 'Głogowska, 60-736, Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'way/100608519', NULL, NULL, 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Sołacki Park', NULL, 'outdoor', 'Park Sołacki – jeden z parków publicznych w Poznaniu, w willowej dzielnicy Sołacz.', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Park_So%C5%82acki_Jesie%C5%84_RB1.JPG?width=1024', 52.4224736, 16.9022922, 'Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'way/335623712', 'pl:Park Sołacki', 'Radomil talk · CC BY-SA 3.0 (via Wikimedia Commons)', 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Lake Rusałka', 'Jezioro Rusałka', 'outdoor', 'Lake Rusałka is an artificial lake in Poznań, Poland. It has an area of 367,000 square metres. It was named after the water nymph Rusalka. It was formed in 1943 as a result of the damming of the Bogdanka River. In 1940 thousands of people were executed in the forests surrounding the lake.', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jezioro_Rusalka_Poznan.jpg?width=1024', 52.4267557, 16.8781252, 'Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'way/22940672', 'en:Lake Rusałka (Poznań)', 'CC BY-SA 3.0 (via Wikimedia Commons)', 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Lake Strzeszyńskie', 'Jezioro Strzeszyńskie', 'outdoor', 'Clean swimming lake popular for summer bathing and cycling.', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', NULL, 52.4607541, 16.822413, 'Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'way/23840021', NULL, NULL, 'osm+wikipedia'),
('Lake Kierskie', 'Jezioro Kierskie', 'outdoor', 'Jezioro Kierskie – jezioro rynnowe polodowcowe, położone w zachodniej części Poznania. Jest to największy zbiornik wodny miasta i jeden z największych w Wielkopolsce. Jezioro leży na terenie Pojezierza Poznańskiego.', NULL, '1h 30min', 'free', 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kierskie_Poznan_2.JPG?width=1024', 52.4573723, 16.7910029, 'Poznan, Poland', NULL, 'way/23428979', 'pl:Jezioro Kierskie', 'via Wikimedia Commons', 'osm+wikipedia'),
